WEBVTT

00:00:01.919 --> 00:00:05.839
Futurama is brought to you
by...Molten Boron.

00:00:05.923 --> 00:00:08.800
Nobody doesn't like Molten Boron

00:00:42.751 --> 00:00:44.545
I hate the Planet of the Moochers.

00:00:44.628 --> 00:00:46.880
They take you out for a drink,
but when the check comes

00:00:46.964 --> 00:00:48.715
their wallet's always in their other pants

00:00:48.799 --> 00:00:50.008
which they borrowed from me.

00:00:51.343 --> 00:00:52.344
Dinner ready?

00:00:52.427 --> 00:00:55.097
Those lousy moochers
cleaned out our pantry.

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:59.434
All they left was baking soda and capers
And here it is.

00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:04.231
Great. We're two days from Earth
with no food.

00:01:04.314 --> 00:01:07.693
Problem solved. You two fight to the death
and I'll cook the loser.

00:01:07.776 --> 00:01:09.444
Work his gut. I like it tender.

00:01:09.528 --> 00:01:11.613
Maybe that planet over there
has a drive-thru.

00:01:11.697 --> 00:01:14.783
A Burger Jerk or a Fishy Joe's
or a Chiseler or something.

00:01:14.867 --> 00:01:17.911
Don't get your hopes up.
We're a billion miles from nowhere.

00:01:17.995 --> 00:01:20.831
Yeah, it's probably
only got a Howard Johnson's.

00:01:25.878 --> 00:01:30.007
Well, it's a type "M" planet,
so it should at least have roddenberries.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.466
I'm experienced at foraging.

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:33.927
I used to find edible mushrooms
on my bath mat.

00:01:34.011 --> 00:01:35.095
I found some rocks.

00:01:35.179 --> 00:01:37.222
- You guys eat rocks, right?
- No.

00:01:37.306 --> 00:01:40.017
Not even if they're sautéed in
a little mud?

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.978
Here's something. It looks like
a ditch full of fried shrimp.

00:01:43.061 --> 00:01:44.146
What are you? Blind?

00:01:44.229 --> 00:01:46.773
It looks more like a hole
full of fried prawns.

00:01:52.404 --> 00:01:55.324
This thing I wear on my wrist
says they're not poisonous.

00:01:57.784 --> 00:01:59.161
Well, how are they?

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:06.793
They're great.

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:09.963
They're like sex, except I'm having them.

00:02:10.589 --> 00:02:13.091
You know what these
would go great with? Rocks.

00:02:13.175 --> 00:02:14.426
Look, here's more.

00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:15.802
The planet's covered with them.

00:02:15.886 --> 00:02:17.679
Let's bring back a couple of pocketfuls.

00:02:17.763 --> 00:02:19.264
No, a whole Bender-ful.

00:02:19.348 --> 00:02:21.183
No, only what we need.

00:02:21.266 --> 00:02:22.267
Stuff the ship.

00:02:28.565 --> 00:02:31.568
Planet Express ship,
you are cleared to land.

00:02:31.652 --> 00:02:32.903
Roger.

00:02:38.033 --> 00:02:40.661
Oh, mon, I'm inhaling these things.

00:02:40.744 --> 00:02:43.080
You guys scored some primo stuff here.

00:02:44.373 --> 00:02:47.042
They're tastier
than an unguarded penguin nest.

00:02:47.125 --> 00:02:48.544
What do you call them?

00:02:48.627 --> 00:02:50.003
We haven't thought of a name yet.

00:02:50.087 --> 00:02:51.505
They're tasty, right?

00:02:51.588 --> 00:02:53.006
Let's call them tasticles.

00:02:54.591 --> 00:02:56.635
- We can't call them that.
- Why not?

00:02:56.718 --> 00:02:57.719
It sounds too much

00:02:57.803 --> 00:03:00.347
Like those frozen Rocky Mountain oysters
on a stick.

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:02.015
You know, testsicles.

00:03:02.808 --> 00:03:06.270
According to government records
the only names not yet trademarked

00:03:06.353 --> 00:03:08.772
are Popplers and Zitsels.

00:03:08.856 --> 00:03:10.524
I know! We'll call them popplers.

00:03:11.525 --> 00:03:12.526
You sure picked it.

00:03:12.609 --> 00:03:13.610
Swish.

00:03:14.653 --> 00:03:17.656
Call them what you want.
I call them a free meal.

00:03:18.699 --> 00:03:19.700
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:03:19.783 --> 00:03:21.285
Slow down there, Sigmund.

00:03:21.368 --> 00:03:24.413
I can't stand idly by
while poor people get free food.

00:03:24.496 --> 00:03:25.789
We gotta sell these things.

00:03:25.873 --> 00:03:27.207
- Yeah!
- Good idea.

00:03:27.291 --> 00:03:28.792
Bender's a genius!

00:03:32.838 --> 00:03:34.506
Hey! Business is great.

00:03:34.882 --> 00:03:37.926
Great is okay, but amazing would be great.

00:03:39.136 --> 00:03:42.181
Please, don't push.
There's hot dogs for everyone.

00:03:44.975 --> 00:03:48.395
Hey, mac, where do you want
those rat droppings you ordered?

00:03:52.816 --> 00:03:53.817
Wait a minute.

00:03:53.901 --> 00:03:56.320
You're not the guy
who delivers the rat droppings.

00:03:57.738 --> 00:04:00.073
What are you selling? Popplers?
Never heard of 'em.

00:04:00.157 --> 00:04:01.700
Eat it or beat it.

00:04:02.951 --> 00:04:03.952
Mmm, mmm.

00:04:04.036 --> 00:04:05.370
These are great.

00:04:05.454 --> 00:04:07.706
Boys, this is your lucky day.

00:04:07.789 --> 00:04:09.208
I'm Joe Gillman.

00:04:09.291 --> 00:04:10.417
Wow.

00:04:10.542 --> 00:04:12.586
You're some guy who eats at Fishy Joe's?

00:04:12.669 --> 00:04:13.712
Hell, no.

00:04:13.795 --> 00:04:15.172
I am Fishy Joe.

00:04:15.255 --> 00:04:18.926
I've got a fast-food franchise
on every planet in the known universe

00:04:19.009 --> 00:04:20.636
Except McPluto.

00:04:20.719 --> 00:04:24.556
Hey, Fishy, I've been meaning to write you
about your in-store kiddie parks.

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:26.600
The slides won't support an adult robot.

00:04:26.683 --> 00:04:28.101
Good point. Not interested.

00:04:28.185 --> 00:04:29.937
But these popplers, these are great.

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:31.188
How much you sell them for?

00:04:31.271 --> 00:04:32.272
A dollar a dozen.

00:04:32.356 --> 00:04:33.899
You'll never make money that way.

00:04:33.982 --> 00:04:37.236
You supply them to me
and I'll sell them for two bucks a dozen

00:04:37.319 --> 00:04:38.487
at my restaurants.

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:40.489
I'll even pay you a dollar a dozen.

00:04:40.572 --> 00:04:41.949
Yes! I'm going to be rich!

00:04:42.032 --> 00:04:44.201
You, too, but it's hard
to get excited about that.

00:04:44.284 --> 00:04:45.285
How do we sign?

00:04:48.247 --> 00:04:50.290
Pop a poppler in your mouth

00:04:50.415 --> 00:04:52.835
When you come to Fishy Joe's
What they're made of is a mystery

00:04:52.918 --> 00:04:55.337
Where they come from, no one knows
You can pick 'em, you can lick 'em

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:57.631
You can chew 'em, you can stick 'em
If you promise not to sue us

00:04:57.714 --> 00:04:59.132
You can shove one up your nose.

00:05:06.807 --> 00:05:08.183
I can't pay.

00:05:23.448 --> 00:05:27.077
Leela, that's the second billboard
you crashed into this week.

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:31.081
Sorry. I was distracted
by those protesters outside our building.

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:44.219
Hey, unless this is a nude love-in

00:05:44.303 --> 00:05:46.013
get the hell off my property.

00:05:46.763 --> 00:05:49.474
You can't own property, man.

00:05:49.558 --> 00:05:52.728
I can, but that's because
I'm not a penniless hippie.

00:05:52.811 --> 00:05:54.313
What do you people want?

00:05:54.396 --> 00:05:57.816
We're with Mankind
for Ethical Animal Treatment.

00:05:57.900 --> 00:05:59.943
Popplers are living creatures.

00:06:00.027 --> 00:06:02.613
You've got to stop
harvesting them for food.

00:06:02.696 --> 00:06:03.697
Or what?

00:06:04.031 --> 00:06:06.408
Or we'll boycott Fishy Joe's.

00:06:06.491 --> 00:06:09.203
You're vegetarians. Who cares what you do?

00:06:09.286 --> 00:06:10.621
Shut up!

00:06:10.704 --> 00:06:13.290
Animals eat other animals. It's nature.

00:06:13.373 --> 00:06:16.460
No, it isn't.
We taught a lion to eat tofu.

00:06:19.588 --> 00:06:22.966
The point is, you shouldn't
eat things that feel pain.

00:06:24.134 --> 00:06:25.761
Okay, we won't eat you.

00:06:25.844 --> 00:06:27.346
I'll go get some more bricks.

00:06:29.264 --> 00:06:32.226
Fry, I wish you'd throw out
these week-old popplers.

00:06:32.309 --> 00:06:34.019
They're getting big and scaly.

00:06:34.478 --> 00:06:35.771
There's one left.

00:06:36.563 --> 00:06:38.357
Mama.

00:06:51.286 --> 00:06:53.413
Stop! Stop eating popplers.

00:06:54.039 --> 00:06:55.415
- Why?
- My booze!

00:06:55.499 --> 00:06:57.042
Popplers are intelligent.

00:06:57.125 --> 00:06:59.211
This one called me "mama."

00:06:59.294 --> 00:07:00.963
Congratulations.

00:07:01.046 --> 00:07:03.131
I assume Amy is the father.

00:07:03.215 --> 00:07:04.883
Popplers can't talk.

00:07:04.967 --> 00:07:06.343
Leela must be hallucinating

00:07:06.426 --> 00:07:08.053
from not eating enough popplers.

00:07:08.136 --> 00:07:09.346
Here, eat some now.

00:07:09.429 --> 00:07:10.430
No!

00:07:10.514 --> 00:07:12.724
- I said eat! Come on! Mangia!
- No!

00:07:13.475 --> 00:07:15.477
Sorry, babies.

00:07:15.561 --> 00:07:17.354
Leela, maybe you should lie down.

00:07:17.437 --> 00:07:19.439
Yes, listen to the father.

00:07:19.523 --> 00:07:21.358
I'm telling you it spoke to me.

00:07:21.441 --> 00:07:22.776
Come on, little poppler.

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:23.861
Say "mama."

00:07:24.903 --> 00:07:28.866
Look, Leela, even if you heard one talk
that doesn't mean it's intelligent.

00:07:28.949 --> 00:07:31.368
I mean, parrots talk,
and we eat them, right?

00:07:31.451 --> 00:07:34.913
Yeah, maybe it just learned
to talk as a parlor trick, like Fry.

00:07:34.997 --> 00:07:36.456
Like Fry, like Fry.

00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:38.834
There's one way, and only one way

00:07:38.917 --> 00:07:41.253
to determine if
an animal is intelligent...

00:07:41.879 --> 00:07:43.714
Dissect its brain.

00:07:43.797 --> 00:07:45.299
No! Mama!

00:07:45.382 --> 00:07:46.884
Stop grandpa!

00:07:48.260 --> 00:07:49.344
Enough chitchat.

00:07:49.428 --> 00:07:51.138
Restrain the specimen.

00:07:54.224 --> 00:07:55.934
...Some of that special sauce.

00:08:03.233 --> 00:08:06.320
Stop eating popplers! They can talk!

00:08:06.403 --> 00:08:08.989
Don't stop to talk. Eat popplers!

00:08:09.072 --> 00:08:10.324
Hey, cut it out.

00:08:10.407 --> 00:08:12.534
Take a coupon. Cut it out.

00:08:12.618 --> 00:08:14.077
Ow! Ooh! Ow!

00:08:20.083 --> 00:08:21.668
People, I won't let you enter.

00:08:21.752 --> 00:08:24.505
Popplers are as intelligent as you or me.

00:08:24.588 --> 00:08:25.672
You, maybe.

00:08:30.427 --> 00:08:32.971
Hear me! Hear me!

00:08:33.055 --> 00:08:34.806
Stop eating popplers!

00:08:34.890 --> 00:08:37.351
Stop eating them with honey mustard sauce!

00:08:37.434 --> 00:08:40.562
Stop eating them
with tangy sweet-and-sour sauce.

00:08:40.646 --> 00:08:43.482
Stop eating the new fiesta poppler salad.

00:08:43.857 --> 00:08:46.944
Stop taking advantage of the
money-saving 12-pack.

00:08:50.656 --> 00:08:55.285
Stop enjoying popplers on the patio,
in the car, or on the boat.

00:08:55.410 --> 00:08:57.371
Wherever good times are had.

00:08:57.955 --> 00:08:59.164
Ow!

00:09:04.169 --> 00:09:06.088
Tonight, on Date Night:

00:09:06.213 --> 00:09:08.006
"Popplers; eating them."

00:09:08.090 --> 00:09:09.216
Is it all right to?

00:09:09.299 --> 00:09:12.052
We have with us the C.E.O. Of Fishy Joe's

00:09:12.135 --> 00:09:13.971
Mr. Fishy Joseph Gillman,

00:09:14.054 --> 00:09:17.766
noted anti-eating activist,
Free Waterfall, Jr.,

00:09:17.850 --> 00:09:21.228
and the discoverer of popplers,
Captain Turanga Leela.

00:09:21.311 --> 00:09:22.312
Turanga?

00:09:22.396 --> 00:09:23.438
That's her name, Phillip.

00:09:23.522 --> 00:09:24.523
Phillip?

00:09:24.606 --> 00:09:27.818
Fishy Joe, is it wrong
to eat intelligent animals?

00:09:27.901 --> 00:09:29.486
Absolutely not, Linda.

00:09:29.611 --> 00:09:31.655
I don't think anyone's here
to make that claim.

00:09:31.738 --> 00:09:33.365
- I am.
- Me, too.

00:09:33.448 --> 00:09:34.449
- Listen...
- Shut up.

00:09:34.533 --> 00:09:36.869
We're talking about a snack
that's low in fat...

00:09:36.952 --> 00:09:38.203
- Shut up.
- ...and high in profit.

00:09:38.287 --> 00:09:40.539
You're crazy, man. He is crazy.

00:09:40.622 --> 00:09:43.876
There's not even any strong evidence
that these popplers are intelligent.

00:09:43.959 --> 00:09:45.419
- Shut up, shut up.
- That's not true.

00:09:45.502 --> 00:09:48.046
- I have one right here that can talk.
- Shut up.

00:09:48.130 --> 00:09:50.507
- Come on. Say "mama."
- Caca.

00:09:50.591 --> 00:09:52.009
Okay, we'll have to bleep that.

00:09:52.092 --> 00:09:55.137
- I'm not saying eating meat is wrong.
- Shut up.

00:09:55.220 --> 00:09:57.973
- No one's here to make that claim.
- I am.

00:09:58.056 --> 00:10:00.350
But eating an intelligent animal
is different.

00:10:00.434 --> 00:10:01.643
Shut up, shut up, shut up.

00:10:01.727 --> 00:10:04.188
Don't force your tired philosophy on us.

00:10:04.271 --> 00:10:06.440
I mean, the only reason
we don't eat people

00:10:06.523 --> 00:10:07.900
is because it tastes lousy.

00:10:07.983 --> 00:10:08.984
You're all nuts.

00:10:09.067 --> 00:10:10.569
Shut up. Let me talk.

00:10:10.652 --> 00:10:11.820
You shut up, please.

00:10:11.904 --> 00:10:13.405
No, you shut up, please.

00:10:13.488 --> 00:10:16.742
Popplers are no smarter than
any other animal I've served,

00:10:16.825 --> 00:10:18.118
and that includes cats.

00:10:18.202 --> 00:10:19.328
Caca-head.

00:10:19.411 --> 00:10:21.580
Mean old caca-head.

00:10:21.663 --> 00:10:23.290
Sir, I'm making a point.

00:10:23.373 --> 00:10:25.959
If these gutter-mouth creatures
are so smart,

00:10:26.043 --> 00:10:27.794
why don't they defend themselves?

00:10:29.755 --> 00:10:30.797
Stop it.

00:10:30.881 --> 00:10:32.799
I call murder on that.

00:10:33.509 --> 00:10:37.137
Look, I'm willing to grant
that it's murder. The real issue is...

00:10:38.096 --> 00:10:39.598
...who's going to stop me?

00:10:49.900 --> 00:10:53.153
We seem to be experiencing
technical difficulties.

00:10:53.237 --> 00:10:55.405
And crap like I've never seen.

00:10:56.490 --> 00:10:58.617
People of earth, I am Lrrr

00:10:58.700 --> 00:11:00.786
of the Planet Omicron Persei 8.

00:11:02.371 --> 00:11:04.331
Turn down the TV, Ndunda.

00:11:04.414 --> 00:11:06.250
Dear lord, they're back.

00:11:06.333 --> 00:11:07.501
We're doomed.

00:11:07.584 --> 00:11:08.877
Doomed!

00:11:09.044 --> 00:11:10.587
)

00:11:10.671 --> 00:11:14.091
Doomed!

00:11:14.174 --> 00:11:16.885
Now then, the creatures you call popplers

00:11:16.969 --> 00:11:19.304
come from a nursery planet in our sector.

00:11:19.972 --> 00:11:22.891
You monsters have been eating our babies.

00:11:28.063 --> 00:11:29.648
We demand justice.

00:11:29.731 --> 00:11:34.236
As you ate our children,
so shall you be eaten by us.

00:11:34.319 --> 00:11:38.115
We will begin with the firemen,
then the math teachers,

00:11:38.198 --> 00:11:41.952
and so on in that fashion
until everyone is eaten.

00:11:45.873 --> 00:11:47.416
Transmission over.

00:11:49.459 --> 00:11:50.878
Well, that went okay.

00:11:50.961 --> 00:11:53.255
I tell you...
when you know you can't scratch

00:11:53.338 --> 00:11:56.258
that's when you really have to, eh?

00:11:56.341 --> 00:11:58.260
Oh, yeah, oh, that feels a lot better.

00:11:58.343 --> 00:12:00.762
What? It's still on? Oh!

00:12:04.433 --> 00:12:06.977
As chief negotiator,
I speak for all of Earth

00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:10.522
when I mourn the
regrettable loss of the omicronian young.

00:12:10.606 --> 00:12:12.316
We share your pain.

00:12:14.193 --> 00:12:15.736
Mmm.

00:12:15.819 --> 00:12:18.363
If we could undo the damage...

00:12:20.991 --> 00:12:22.784
These would be great with gwack-a-mole.

00:12:22.868 --> 00:12:24.119
Stop eating our young!

00:12:24.203 --> 00:12:25.662
And it's pronounced guacamole!

00:12:26.663 --> 00:12:28.373
All right. I'm putting them away.

00:12:32.794 --> 00:12:34.379
Now, what is it you want?

00:12:34.463 --> 00:12:36.006
We demand...

00:12:36.089 --> 00:12:37.758
We demand to eat

00:12:37.841 --> 00:12:39.885
one human for each omicronian
that was eaten.

00:12:39.968 --> 00:12:41.929
Fair enough. How many is that?

00:12:42.846 --> 00:12:45.390
Hundred and ninety-eight billion, Sir.

00:12:45.474 --> 00:12:46.475
Very well.

00:12:46.558 --> 00:12:50.395
You will provide us
with 198 billion humans

00:12:50.479 --> 00:12:51.855
And small fries.

00:12:51.939 --> 00:12:53.065
Lrrr!

00:12:53.148 --> 00:12:55.317
Oh, all right, cottage cheese.

00:12:55.400 --> 00:12:58.445
Sir, there aren't
that many human beings.

00:12:58.529 --> 00:12:59.780
A thought occurs.

00:12:59.863 --> 00:13:01.657
There aren't that many humans.

00:13:01.740 --> 00:13:04.284
We'll wait a few weeks
while you shore up the numbers.

00:13:05.118 --> 00:13:07.871
One hundred ninety-eight billion babies
in a few weeks.

00:13:07.955 --> 00:13:11.750
We'll need an army of super-virile men
scoring 'round the clock!

00:13:11.834 --> 00:13:13.168
I'll do my part.

00:13:13.252 --> 00:13:15.003
Kif, clear my schedule.

00:13:19.258 --> 00:13:22.219
I wish they'd just wipe out humanity
and get it over with.

00:13:22.302 --> 00:13:23.971
It's the waiting I can't stand.

00:13:24.054 --> 00:13:25.138
That's stupid.

00:13:31.854 --> 00:13:35.148
My fellow earthlings,
we have reached an agreement.

00:13:35.232 --> 00:13:37.985
Using the twin guns of grace and tact

00:13:38.068 --> 00:13:41.864
I blasted our worthless enemies
with a fair compromise.

00:13:43.323 --> 00:13:45.033
They will not eat everyone on Earth.

00:13:45.117 --> 00:13:47.995
I filled up on nuts at the negotiation.

00:13:48.078 --> 00:13:51.915
Instead, they will eat only
a single human of their choice.

00:13:51.999 --> 00:13:55.752
We choose to eat the first earthling
who ate our offspring.

00:13:55.836 --> 00:13:57.129
Here is the culprit

00:13:57.212 --> 00:13:59.548
As photographed
by our nanny-cam satellite.

00:14:01.300 --> 00:14:02.885
She must be sacrificed,

00:14:02.968 --> 00:14:05.971
but the rest of you shall be spared.

00:14:08.390 --> 00:14:09.641
Boo!

00:14:09.725 --> 00:14:11.768
Boo!

00:14:23.780 --> 00:14:28.994
Tonight the world watches in horror
as an earthling is eaten alive

00:14:29.077 --> 00:14:30.454
on network television.

00:14:30.537 --> 00:14:35.876
This grim scene of unimaginable carnage
is brought to you by Fishy Joe's.

00:14:35.959 --> 00:14:38.212
Try our new extreme walrus juice.

00:14:38.879 --> 00:14:41.840
100% fresh-squeezed walrus.

00:14:41.924 --> 00:14:43.175
Ride the walrus.

00:14:43.258 --> 00:14:46.178
Ladies and gentlemen

00:14:46.261 --> 00:14:49.640
The omicronians!

00:14:51.975 --> 00:14:54.061
Greetings, earth morsels.

00:14:55.521 --> 00:14:56.980
You suck!

00:14:57.064 --> 00:14:58.148
Get a job!

00:14:58.232 --> 00:15:00.484
I'll miss you, Leela.

00:15:00.567 --> 00:15:02.986
I know you're just
a carbon-based life-form

00:15:03.070 --> 00:15:04.988
but I'll always think of you

00:15:05.072 --> 00:15:08.075
as a big pile of titanium.

00:15:08.158 --> 00:15:10.786
What Bender means is, you're really brave,

00:15:10.869 --> 00:15:13.455
and smart, and beautiful,
and a great friend.

00:15:13.539 --> 00:15:15.332
Just like titanium.

00:15:18.418 --> 00:15:20.128
This is all a big load.

00:15:20.212 --> 00:15:22.840
I was the one trying to save the popplers.

00:15:22.923 --> 00:15:25.592
You were sucking them down
like the fat hog you are,

00:15:25.676 --> 00:15:27.970
and you were stepping on them for fun.

00:15:29.388 --> 00:15:32.057
You both should be in here instead of me.

00:15:32.140 --> 00:15:34.226
Someone's acting awfully aluminum.

00:15:34.309 --> 00:15:36.311
Leela, my sweet, I've come to save you.

00:15:36.395 --> 00:15:37.980
I have a devious plan.

00:15:38.063 --> 00:15:41.525
Oh, great. Captain Moron has a plan.

00:15:41.608 --> 00:15:44.027
Why don't you tell it to wingus
and dingus here?

00:15:44.111 --> 00:15:45.696
Wingus, dingus, listen up.

00:15:45.779 --> 00:15:48.532
We're going to give the aliens
the old switcheroo.

00:15:48.615 --> 00:15:49.741
- You mean...
- Correct.

00:15:49.825 --> 00:15:51.285
I found a giant, hideous ape

00:15:51.368 --> 00:15:53.120
that looks exactly like Leela.

00:15:56.540 --> 00:15:58.584
It doesn't look anything like me.

00:15:58.667 --> 00:16:00.085
The hair is all wrong.

00:16:00.169 --> 00:16:02.629
Don't worry, Kif is an expert stylist,

00:16:02.713 --> 00:16:04.131
as you can plainly see.

00:16:04.214 --> 00:16:05.799
Mmm!

00:16:13.515 --> 00:16:16.059
You know, this might actually work.

00:16:16.143 --> 00:16:19.479
The omicronians seem to have trouble
telling one person from another.

00:16:19.563 --> 00:16:21.982
True. At the negotiations,
they thought Kif here

00:16:22.065 --> 00:16:24.943
was the statesman
and I was a jabbering mental patient.

00:16:25.027 --> 00:16:26.236
Isn't that right, Kif?

00:16:26.320 --> 00:16:28.739
Please, I'm creating.

00:16:31.533 --> 00:16:33.118
Voilà!

00:16:35.746 --> 00:16:37.331
- Bingo!
- That' Leela.

00:16:37.414 --> 00:16:38.749
I'm seeing double.

00:16:40.542 --> 00:16:41.877
I grow hungry.

00:16:41.960 --> 00:16:44.880
Bring on the one called "Leela."

00:16:44.963 --> 00:16:47.132
That comes with salad or soup.

00:16:47.216 --> 00:16:48.217
Salad.

00:16:48.300 --> 00:16:49.426
Ranch or vinaigrette?

00:16:49.510 --> 00:16:50.511
Vinaigrette.

00:16:50.594 --> 00:16:52.221
Balsamic or raspberry?

00:17:05.275 --> 00:17:06.693
People of earth...

00:17:06.777 --> 00:17:08.153
Shh!

00:17:10.113 --> 00:17:11.198
Hmm.

00:17:11.281 --> 00:17:14.660
Hmm. Mmm-hmm.

00:17:16.954 --> 00:17:19.498
Yes, this is the one, definitely.

00:17:19.581 --> 00:17:22.876
I recognize her slumping posture
and hairy knuckles.

00:17:33.136 --> 00:17:35.931
Would you like some human with your salt?

00:17:39.643 --> 00:17:40.644
This is it.

00:17:40.727 --> 00:17:42.938
If the aliens fall for Zapp's ploy

00:17:43.021 --> 00:17:44.648
the Earth will be saved.

00:17:44.731 --> 00:17:46.608
Brought to you by Fishy Joe's.

00:17:46.692 --> 00:17:47.860
"Ride the walrus."

00:17:53.448 --> 00:17:54.867
Wait! Stop!

00:17:54.950 --> 00:17:57.077
It's a trick! That's not Leela!

00:17:58.203 --> 00:18:00.330
What's happening? I'm losing the crowd.

00:18:00.414 --> 00:18:02.040
It's an orangutan.

00:18:02.124 --> 00:18:05.335
One of Mother Earth's
most precious creatures.

00:18:06.336 --> 00:18:08.005
Hmm.

00:18:11.425 --> 00:18:14.761
Why'd you open your bonghole,
you smelly hippie?

00:18:14.845 --> 00:18:18.515
You'd sacrifice a beautiful woman
to save a moderately attractive monkey?

00:18:18.599 --> 00:18:21.435
You must've smoked some bad granola.

00:18:21.518 --> 00:18:24.313
The one called "smelly hippie" is right.

00:18:24.396 --> 00:18:25.898
This is a monkey.

00:18:27.065 --> 00:18:29.109
Yes, definitely.

00:18:29.860 --> 00:18:31.737
Where is the real female?

00:18:31.820 --> 00:18:32.946
I'll never tell.

00:18:33.030 --> 00:18:34.615
Where is the real female?

00:18:34.698 --> 00:18:36.033
I'll get her for you.

00:18:37.743 --> 00:18:42.039
I realize this may hurt our chances
of consummating our relationship again.

00:18:42.122 --> 00:18:43.373
Go consummate yourself.

00:18:43.457 --> 00:18:45.667
Stop talking! You're getting cold!

00:18:46.835 --> 00:18:49.463
Please! I just paid off my car!

00:18:49.546 --> 00:18:51.632
- No!
- I can't look.

00:18:57.054 --> 00:18:58.263
Stop!

00:19:02.267 --> 00:19:03.977
People of Earth.

00:19:04.061 --> 00:19:08.023
I am Jrrr of the planet Omicron Persei 8.

00:19:08.106 --> 00:19:09.816
Could someone lower this thing for me?

00:19:10.817 --> 00:19:13.237
Now, then, if Leela gets eaten

00:19:13.320 --> 00:19:14.571
I get eaten!

00:19:15.864 --> 00:19:18.242
Little one, get out of there!

00:19:18.325 --> 00:19:20.369
I'm going to count to blarks.

00:19:20.452 --> 00:19:21.995
But elder one...

00:19:22.079 --> 00:19:26.875
Flingle, glorg, glorg-and-a-gloob...

00:19:26.959 --> 00:19:28.043
Hear me out!

00:19:28.126 --> 00:19:30.212
There are many good reasons to eat:

00:19:30.295 --> 00:19:32.840
Hunger, boredom,

00:19:32.923 --> 00:19:35.259
wanting to be the world's fattest man,

00:19:35.342 --> 00:19:36.718
but not revenge.

00:19:36.802 --> 00:19:38.637
Are we no better than they?

00:19:38.720 --> 00:19:41.265
Besides, Leela's my friend.

00:19:41.348 --> 00:19:43.058
Is this true, earthling?

00:19:44.768 --> 00:19:48.146
Leela's garbled words have opened my eyes.

00:19:53.694 --> 00:19:55.195
Okay, that's a start.

00:19:55.279 --> 00:19:57.322
That's very earth-friendly.

00:19:57.406 --> 00:19:59.575
Now, everyone join hands!

00:19:59.658 --> 00:20:00.909
Join hands, please!

00:20:00.993 --> 00:20:03.161
I'd like to lead you all in some swaying.

00:20:03.245 --> 00:20:04.454
Come on. Pay attention.

00:20:05.747 --> 00:20:07.457
I said do it!

00:20:07.541 --> 00:20:09.459
- Yeah.
- Is he your friend, too?

00:20:09.543 --> 00:20:10.794
No.

00:20:10.878 --> 00:20:11.920
Aah!

00:20:12.004 --> 00:20:13.422
This is not happening.

00:20:18.510 --> 00:20:21.263
I think there was
something funny in that hippie.

00:20:21.346 --> 00:20:23.015
Thank you, Jrrr.

00:20:23.348 --> 00:20:25.893
I hope you'll always
think of me as your mom.

00:20:25.976 --> 00:20:28.896
When my species grows up, we eat our moms.

00:20:28.979 --> 00:20:30.230
Whoop!

00:20:30.355 --> 00:20:31.815
People of earth...

00:20:31.899 --> 00:20:34.234
That hippie's starting to kick in.

00:20:34.735 --> 00:20:37.404
We've all learned
an important lesson today.

00:20:37.487 --> 00:20:39.656
I realize now that...

00:20:40.490 --> 00:20:43.827
Dude, my hands are huge.

00:20:46.288 --> 00:20:49.374
They can touch anything but themselves.

00:20:49.958 --> 00:20:51.043
Oh, wait.

00:20:51.126 --> 00:20:52.294
Let's go.

00:20:55.297 --> 00:20:56.590
Ooh.

00:20:56.673 --> 00:20:58.800
Hmm?

00:20:59.968 --> 00:21:01.929
Whoa-ho-ho.

00:21:02.012 --> 00:21:03.430
Whoo.

00:21:03.805 --> 00:21:05.057
Yeah...

00:21:09.645 --> 00:21:11.772
I feel like I'm flying.

00:21:17.277 --> 00:21:18.820
A toast to Leela.

00:21:18.904 --> 00:21:21.907
She showed us it's wrong
to eat certain things.

00:21:21.990 --> 00:21:23.867
- Hear, hear!
- Let's get drunk!

00:21:23.951 --> 00:21:25.410
Aw! Thanks, guys.

00:21:25.494 --> 00:21:27.538
- Pass the veal, please.
- Here you go.

00:21:27.788 --> 00:21:30.374
Mmm. Let me get some of that suckling pig.

00:21:31.375 --> 00:21:32.417
Who wants dolphin?

00:21:32.543 --> 00:21:34.294
Dolphin?

00:21:34.378 --> 00:21:35.879
But dolphins are intelligent.

00:21:35.963 --> 00:21:37.047
Not this one.

00:21:37.130 --> 00:21:39.424
He blew all his money
on instant lottery tickets.

00:21:39.883 --> 00:21:41.134
- Oh!
- That's different.

00:21:41.218 --> 00:21:42.344
Pass the blowhole.

00:21:42.427 --> 00:21:43.428
Can I have a fluke?

00:21:43.512 --> 00:21:45.097
Hey, quit hoggin' the bottlenose.

00:21:45.180 --> 00:21:48.058
Toss me the speech center of the brain.